HOW TO USE
  1. Copy to `.agents/rules/<rule-name>.md` (kebab-case, e.g. `logging.md`,
     `data-privacy.md`, `performance.md`).
  2. Fill every <PLACEHOLDER>. Delete any section that genuinely doesn't apply.
  3. Add a pointer in the root `AGENTS.md` under "Detailed rules", e.g.:
       - Logging & observability → `.agents/rules/logging.md`
  4. Keep it tight: rules and "don'ts" first, rationale last. Reference the root
     always-on rules instead of restating them.

DESIGN NOTES
  - A good rule file answers: when does this apply, what must/must not happen,
    and how does the agent verify it followed the rule.
  - Prefer copy-pasteable specifics (commands, exact names) over vague prose.
  - If a rule needs per-language variants, put those in `.agents/rules/lang/`.
