# <RULE NAME> rules

> Applies to: <SCOPE — path globs, task types, or "all work in this repo">
> Relates to: <OTHER RULES this extends or depends on, e.g. `secrets.md`; or "N/A">

## Rule

- <THE CORE REQUIREMENT stated as an imperative, e.g. "Use structured logging.">
- <ADD as many concrete, checkable requirements as needed.>

## Do

- <SPECIFIC ALLOWED/EXPECTED practice, with exact tools/commands/names where possible.>

## Don't

- <SPECIFIC PROHIBITED practice. Tie to a root rule where relevant, e.g. fail-fast, no empty try/catch.>

## How to verify

- <HOW the agent confirms compliance before declaring done — a command, a check,
  or a review step. Ties into the Definition of done.>

## Rationale

- <WHY this rule exists — the failure it prevents. Keep to 1–3 lines.>
